    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract logic and real-world patterns—something I enjoy solving puzzles for. My parents taught me early that it’s not just about memorization but understanding concepts deeply, which aligns with my love for history (patterns in time) and chemistry (structures behind elements). Though I’m still learning, I find its precision rewarding.",
